From 24112704a21b378f88b9be82f5885fd3e771b26e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:20:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FPU F2: arithmetic and compare -- x87 computes

Phase F2 of docs/plans/FPU_PLAN.md lands the numeric surface.  The raw
operand-direction probes (/tmp/rawdir, encodings executed as db bytes
because GAS swaps the fsubp/fsubrp mnemonics) confirm the SDM map: D8
register forms compute OP ST(0),ST(i) into ST0, DC forms OP
ST(i),ST(0) into ST(i), DE forms do the same and pop, FSUBR/FDIVR swap
the values, and the D8/DC/DA/DE memory forms share the non-reversed
/4-/7 map (DC /4 = FSUB m64).  Every numeric op runs on the host x87
itself -- volatile long double expressions for the binary group, raw
encodings for fsqrt/frndint/fprem/fprem1/fscale/fxtract -- so result
bits and NaN patterns are silicon-exact, and fesetround(FCW.RC) runs
first so rounding follows the guest control word.

The compare families (FCOM/FCOMP/FCOMPP, FUCOM/FUCOMP/FUCOMPP,
FICOM/FICOMP, and the EFLAGS forms FCOMI/FCOMIP/FUCOMI/FUCOMIP) follow
the host-measured NaN matrix (/tmp/cmpmat): FCOM* raise IE on any NaN,
FUCOM* only on SNaN; unordered gives C0=C2=C3=1 or CF=PF=ZF=1; a
denormal source sets DE and compares normally.  FXTRACT is
host-measured too: after the push ST0 holds the significand and ST1 the
unbiased exponent.  FPREM/FPREM1 copy the instruction's quotient flags
(C0=Q2 C3=Q1 C1=Q0, C2 marks partial steps).

The compare probes also caught defect D6: the F1 FSW/FCW exception-bit
map was reversed.  Isolated host probes (/tmp/flagbits, FNCLEX per op)
measure IE=0x0001 DE=0x0002 ZE=0x0004 OE=0x0008 UE=0x0010 PE=0x0020
with the FCW masks mirroring the order (IM=bit0..PM=bit5); overflow
sets OE+PE, underflow UE+PE, denormal-operand DE alone.  The F1
vectors that pinned the wrong bits are corrected in this commit and
v_d6_flag_map locks the measured order.  A related receipt: FLD
m32/m64 of an SNaN quiets it and raises IE (converting load), while
FLD m80 is a pure move (SNaN preserved, no exception).

Vectors: tests/test_fpu.c F2 suites (33 groups): direction pins vs
host-computed long double results, 1/0 -> +inf + ZE and 0/0 -> real
indefinite + IE with #MF delivery for unmasked ZM/DM, FPREM flag
receipts, FXTRACT layout, compare/COMI matrices through QNaN and SNaN
(m80 loads keep an SNaN signaling so the FUCOM rule is testable), and
the D6 pins.  Negative control: faulting the F2 escapes again reddens
46 checks.  The frozen T-row is narrowed per the V5 recipe -- the pin
moves with the phases (D9 C0 fell with F1, D8 C1 with F2) and now
sits on the F3 edge: D9 F0 (F2XM1) stays #UD.

Gates: make test green (test-fpu: ok; guest lanes byte-stable -- the
sample firmware never executes x87), make test-sanitize green,
diff-fuzz 512 programs / 12 288 instructions all-match with zero
host-level crashes, SeaBIOS ISO lanes green (Q MBR 10.4 s, C El Torito
10.0 s).  FPU_PLAN.md gains the F2 measured receipts; STATUS.md and
CHANGELOG are synced.
